{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration and recovery policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear priority to forward progress in clear space, uses occasional random_walk for coverage diversity, handles obstacle_front via brief backward escape then directed turn, handles obstacle_left/right via consistent short directed turns, and reserves full_rotate only for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage. Action states are one-shot, obstacle states never enable forward/random_walk, and uncontrollable events are total in every specification state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and place the task policy in specification automata",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward with occasional random_walk, while making obstacle recovery brief, directed, and one-shot",
    "Use a dedicated front-obstacle recovery chain with rare move_backward and a dedicated stuck/last_resort path for full_rotate only after repeated blocked conditions",
    "Make action/commit states robust to open-loop pulse semantics by self-looping on path_clear and only letting obstacle events preempt when safety-critical"
  ],
